fields.value:
 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Power Cogs icon0}}
| desc = Forms a ring of energized cogs around Clockwerk, trapping any units that are near. Enemies outside the trap that touch a cog are knocked back, losing health and mana. Once a cog has delivered a shock, it will power down. Damage is increased by 50% of the mana burned.<br><br>Cogs can be destroyed by enemy attacks, but Clockwerk can push them up to 850 distance away with one hit. Clockwerk can move through the cogs freely, disabling them as he passes over.
}}
<hr>
* [[File:Dota2 Clockwerk Power Cogs Formation icon.png|84px|Power Cogs Formation]]
** Each Power Cog is created at an equal distance away at point [[File:Dota2 Letter-s.png|21px|S]] from centerpoint [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|21px|O]].
*** {{Code|OS {{=}} OS' {{=}} {{#var:Power Cogs value1}}}}
*** [[File:Dota2 Clockwerk Power Cogs Calculation icon.png|105px]]
**** Point [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|21px|P]] and [[File:Dota2 Letter-q.png|21px|Q]] are the centerpoint of two Power Cogs respectively.
**** {{Code|PQ {{=}} SpawnDistance × [[Wikipedia:Square root|√]] (2 - √ (2)) {{=}} {{#expr:{{#var:Power Cogs value1}}*(sqrt(2-sqrt(2))) round2}}}}
*** Line [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]] indicates the remaining gap between the Power Cogs.
*** {{Symbol|Bound Radius}}
**** With an {{Show|U|Power Cog|bound radius}}-[[bound radius]], the remaining gap ({{Code|F}}) between two Power Cogs has {{Code|{{#expr:{{#var:Power Cogs gap}}}}-distance}}.
**** Hence, only the following units can pass through the {{M|pathing blocker}}:
***** Has a {{Code|< F}} bound radius value.
***** While affected by {{M|unobstructed movement}} sources.

* Although creeps do not attack the Power Cogs, they can destroy the cogs with 4 attacks.

* {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
** {{Symbol|Attack Damage}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|rattletrap_cog_pinball}}
*** Attacking the moving Power Cog again refreshes the forced movement duration.
**** However, this neither affects its forced movement distance nor the traveling speed. The Cog stops at its original predetermined position and does not attempt to move again.
**** The buff applied has to expire for the forced movement to be reapplied again on the Power Cog.
** {{Symbol|Ranged}}
*** For [[ranged]] heroes, the applied {{M|forced movement}} direction checks for the caster's position upon a successful attack projectile impact, and the {{U|Power Cog}} moves in a straight line accordingly to the caster's {{M|facing angle}}.

